1
# C# File Creation Using Windows Forms

## Description
This project demonstrates how to create a text file using C# Windows Forms.

## How It Works
When the user clicks the Create File button, the program creates a file named `Test.txt`. It then writes my name, university, faculty, and age into the file using the `StreamWriter` class.

After saving the information, the program closes the file and displays a message to confirm that the file was created successfully.


2

# C# Read Text File Using Windows Forms

## Description
This project demonstrates how to read information from a text file using C# Windows Forms.

## How It Works
When the user clicks the Read File button, the program checks whether `Test.txt` exists. If the file is found, it reads all the lines using `File.ReadAllLines()` and displays them in a ListBox.

If the file does not exist, the program displays a message asking the user to create the file first. The `try-catch` block handles errors that may occur during the process.

3

# C# Delete File Using Windows Forms

## Description
This project demonstrates how to delete a text file using C# Windows Forms.

## How It Works
When the user clicks the Delete File button, the program checks whether `Test.txt` exists. If the file exists, it deletes the file using `File.Delete()` and clears all items from the ListBox.

If the file does not exist, the program displays a message. The `try-catch` block is used to handle errors.

4

# C# Delete Selected Item from File

## Description
This project uses C# Windows Forms to delete a selected item from a ListBox and update the text file.

## How It Works
The program checks whether the user has selected an item in the ListBox. If an item is selected, it removes the item, saves the remaining items back to `Test.txt`, and displays a success message.

If no item is selected, the program asks the user to select an item first. The `try-catch` block handles errors.
